{
  "note": "The fixed question set the live parity harness runs through both clients. Each entry is one head: a Noul, a Choice, or a Score. `gate` overrides the think gate for that question, which is how the thinking read is exercised without sending every other question through a thought. `image` makes the question an image question: it is a data URL so both clients send the same bytes and neither needs a file the other can see. An endpoint that does not serve images skips that case rather than failing it; see docs/PORT.md.",
  "evidence_note": "`evidence` is the JSON value the readout serializes into the prompt, so it is the same bytes on both sides.",
